# Optional. Copy this file to keys.env (same directory) and fill in what you
# have - .free-agents/setup.sh reads it once and writes each key straight into
# that agent's OWN config file (not into this tool's registry, which never
# stores raw keys - see docs/SETUP.md). Leave any line blank to skip it; the
# agent still works without it, either with no credential at all (kilo) or
# via its own interactive login (opencode: `opencode auth login`).
#
# keys.env is gitignored. It never leaves this machine and this file commits
# no secret - only the blank template does.
#
# IMPORTANT: use a DIFFERENT OpenRouter key on every line below that you fill
# in. The same key pasted twice is not two lanes, it is ONE wallet racing
# itself for the same rate limit - the entire point of this tool is credential
# = lane, and a repeated key defeats it. setup.sh warns if it catches this,
# but the warning can only compare what you gave it - get free keys (one per
# line, from different OpenRouter accounts if you want all three) at
# https://openrouter.ai/keys

OPENCODE_OPENROUTER_KEY=
KILO_OPENROUTER_KEY=
PI_OPENROUTER_KEY=
